# AI-ASM AArch64 v0.5 - Development Prompt

## Project Overview
Pure AArch64 assembly OS kernel with embedded Wasm3 runtime, running on QEMU virt (128MB RAM) on Termux.

## Build Commands
```bash
make all      # Build full kernel.elf
make clean    # Remove build artifacts
make run      # Build and launch in QEMU
make modules  # Build WASM modules only
make wasm3    # Build wasm3 library only
```

## Architecture
- Boot: kernel.asm -> wasm_host_init_multi() -> load init module -> run ready modules
- Multi-module WASM runtime: shared IM3Environment, per-module IM3Runtime
- RAM disk: embedded USTAR TAR with read-only filesystem
- Module lifecycle: FREE -> LOADING -> READY -> RUNNING -> EXITED

## Key Files
- kernel/kernel.asm - Boot sequence and entry point
- kernel/wasm_host.c - WASM runtime host functions and module management
- kernel/module_runtime.h - Multi-module runtime data structures
- kernel/ramdisk.asm - Embeds WASM modules and RAM disk TAR
- modules/init/src/main.c - Init module (spawns other modules)
- modules/shell/src/main.c - Interactive shell with filesystem commands

## Shell Commands
help, tick, echo, alloc, log, clear, ls, cat, exit
